KG42.register("nodes-04455bbd101c398fd3720a2a",{"id":"COMP-4c1817f6cddf8a9c","code":"CLR036","label":"Equilibrium allocation of electricity and shared-storage capacity with a high-price scarcity case","definition":"Includes equilibrium allocation and instance-result properties: the aggregator solves for the market equilibrium, determines bilateral transaction quantities, and allocates buyer SES capacity; the transaction quantities satisfy \\sum_{b\\in B}p^t_{sb}\\le P^t_s, p^t_{sb}\\ge0, and \\sum_{s\\in S}p^t_{sb}+p^t_{bg}+p^t_{bd}=D^t_b+p^t_{bc}, p^t_{bg}\\ge0. Additionally, in a supply-scarcity instance, buyers with higher transaction prices obtain limited electrical energy.","layer":"L5","template_code":"BCT","concept_id":"clearing.local","concept_ids":["clearing.local"],"identity_dimensions":{"identity_fields":["Allocation object: bilateral P2P transaction quantities and buyer SES capacity","Core allocation relation: the market equilibrium composed of each agent's optimality conditions, and the resource feasibility constraints","Allocation output: transaction quantities and capacity allocation","Independent result property: in a scarcity instance, higher-price buyers obtain limited electrical energy"]},"exclusions":["Initial seller residual quantity P^t_s and buyer demand D^t_b","Buyer grid electricity purchases and SES charging and discharging jointly enter the energy balance","The source text uses concatenation of KKT conditions, Big-M linearization, and MILP solving","The scarcity result is limited to t=8 and t=18 of Case 3","The unit does not expand the SES capacity-allocation constraints"],"members":[{"id":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","market_meaning":"The aggregator performs local P2P market clearing. Scope: Proposed local P2P energy market embedded with residential shared energy storage. In these scarcity examples, buyers offering higher P2P transaction prices acquire the limited energy. Scope: Reported Case 3 market-equilibrium examples at t = 8 and t = 18. Condition: Total buyer energy demand exceeds total energy supply, and buyers compete for limited energy. A seller’s total P2P transaction amount cannot exceed its initial surplus energy in that period. Scope: Each energy seller and each period in the proposed P2P equilibrium model. Bilateral P2P transaction amounts must be nonnegative. Scope: Every seller–buyer P2P transaction amount in every period. P2P purchases plus grid purchases plus SES discharge must equal the buyer’s energy demand plus SES charging; grid purchases must be nonnegative. Scope: Each energy buyer and each period in the proposed P2P equilibrium model.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Each energy buyer and each period in the proposed P2P equilibrium model. | Each energy seller and each period in the proposed P2P equilibrium model. | Every seller–buyer P2P transaction amount in every period. | Proposed local P2P energy market embedded with residential shared energy storage. | Reported Case 3 market-equilibrium examples at t = 8 and t = 18.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g03-e12","v141-b-g03-e13"]},"constraint_refs":["49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C001","49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C002","49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C003","49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C004","49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C005"],"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","source_rule_sha256":"5b0a6ea74646d677bac9ef5735b8532211f481cb19f837d9ad545e0e8fd0cc2c","paper":"49-residential_shared_storage_market","rule_ref":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001","node_id":"clearing.local","function":"clearing.local","unit_id":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-a-M01::clearing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":true},{"id":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R008::V::clearing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","market_meaning":"Solving the local market equilibrium determines P2P transaction allocations and produces the endogenous bilateral transaction prices. Scope: Bilateral seller–buyer transactions in the proposed local P2P market embedded with residential shared energy storage. The P2P transaction price must be no less than the feed-in tariff plus the P2P transaction cost and no greater than TLOU. Scope: Bilateral P2P transaction prices in the proposed model. No single participant unilaterally controls the P2P clearing price. Scope: The proposed local P2P pricing mechanism.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Bilateral P2P transaction prices in the proposed model. | Bilateral seller–buyer transactions in the proposed local P2P market embedded with residential shared energy storage. | The proposed local P2P pricing mechanism.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g03-e03","v141-b-g03-e04"]},"constraint_refs":["49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C001"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"cb8bb8165d1e8d357b66c34b44b5c95ee431f6bab35f04fb44df80f24044ce4d","paper":"49-residential_shared_storage_market","rule_ref":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R008","node_id":"clearing.local","function":"clearing.local","unit_id":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-a-M01::clearing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false}],"paper_ids":["49-residential_shared_storage_market"],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p05-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.3 Aggregator","anchor_text":"Since the energy buyers use the SES, the allocation of SES use right is also a game. In practice, th","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The aggregator collects all participants’ supply and demand information and clears the P2P market. By solving the market equilibrium problem, it can provide P2P transaction price and amount between energy seller and buyer and capacity allocation among energy buyers. The aggregator can facilitate the P2P market and make sure participants benefit from the market.","paper":"49-residential_shared_storage_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"The aggregator collects all participants’ supply and demand information and clears the P2P market. By solving the market equilibrium problem, it can provide P2P transaction price and amount between energy seller and buyer and capacity allocation among energy buyers. The aggregator can facilitate the P2P market and make sure participants benefit from the market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p10-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":10,"printed_page":null,"section":"5.2.2 Peer-to-peer market equilibrium","anchor_text":"m. as shown in Fig. 3c. However, during the generation peak time, total al supply exceeds total dema","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-10.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"To further show the results of P2P transactions, we pick up 4 typical periods to analyze the P2P market equilibrium in Case 3, as shown in Table 4. The transaction pair is (ρ^{t}_{sb}, p^{t}_{st}), indicating the P2P transaction price and amount between seller s and buyer b during period t. The supply is the PV generation, while the demand is the initial fixed demand plus/minus charging/discharging power of shared energy storage. TLOU0 is the base price faced by buyers when purchasing electricity from the grid. FiT is the Feed-in Tariff offered by the grid. In our model, the P2P transaction price and amount are obtained from solving the market equilibrium problem.","paper":"49-residential_shared_storage_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"To further show the results of P2P transactions, we pick up 4 typical periods to analyze the P2P market equilibrium in Case 3, as shown in Table 4. The transaction pair is (ρ^{t}_{sb}, p^{t}_{st}), indicating the P2P transaction price and amount between seller s and buyer b during period t. The supply is the PV generation, while the demand is the initial fixed demand plus/minus charging/discharging power of shared energy storage. TLOU0 is the base price faced by buyers when purchasing electricity from the grid. FiT is the Feed-in Tariff offered by the grid. In our model, the P2P transaction price and amount are obtained from solving the market equilibrium problem."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e13","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p10-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":10,"printed_page":null,"section":"5.2.2 Peer-to-peer market equilibrium","anchor_text":"market equilibrium problem. Table 4 provides a direct insight into how ac market equilibrium arises.","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-10.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"When t = 8, the PV generation is small, so the total energy demand among energy buyers exceeds the total energy supply. In such a circumstance, all buyers will compete for the limited energy resource. Buyers offering higher transaction prices will acquire the limited energy, e.g., B3 with the highest price 0.1814. Actually, the price 0.1814 is also the marginal cost when B3 buys electricity from the grid to satisfy the unmet needs after the P2P transaction. The same analysis works at t = 18 time period.","paper":"49-residential_shared_storage_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"When t = 8, the PV generation is small, so the total energy demand among energy buyers exceeds the total energy supply. In such a circumstance, all buyers will compete for the limited energy resource. Buyers offering higher transaction prices will acquire the limited energy, e.g., B3 with the highest price 0.1814. Actually, the price 0.1814 is also the marginal cost when B3 buys electricity from the grid to satisfy the unmet needs after the P2P transaction. The same analysis works at t = 18 time period."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E14","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1 Seller’s problem","anchor_text":"he ergy buyers in the P2P market. The second term is the revenue of selling an energy to the power g","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"restatement"},"source_text":"The objective of each energy seller is to maximize its profit. In the objective function (1), the first term is the revenue of trading with energy buyers in the P2P market. The second term is the revenue of selling energy to the power grid in the FiT scheme. After participating in the P2P transaction, energy seller can still sell their surplus to the power grid to get more income. The third term is the transaction cost for P2P transactions. Constraint (2) stipulates that total P2P transaction amounts in period t should not exceed the seller’s initial excessive energy. Constraint (3) is for the non-negativity condition for the decision variable p^{t}_{sb}. \\upsilon^{t}_{s} and \\omega^{t}_{sb} after the colon are dual variables of the constraints.","paper":"49-residential_shared_storage_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"The objective of each energy seller is to maximize its profit. In the objective function (1), the first term is the revenue of trading with energy buyers in the P2P market. The second term is the revenue of selling energy to the power grid in the FiT scheme. After participating in the P2P transaction, energy seller can still sell their surplus to the power grid to get more income. The third term is the transaction cost for P2P transactions. Constraint (2) stipulates that total P2P transaction amounts in period t should not exceed the seller’s initial excessive energy. Constraint (3) is for the non-negativity condition for the decision variable p^{t}_{sb}. \\upsilon^{t}_{s} and \\omega^{t}_{sb} after the colon are dual variables of the constraints."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1 Seller’s problem","anchor_text":"gy , pi to decision-making problem can be cast as ∑ ∑ ∑ ∑ e. max : ( ρtsbptsb + λtsell(Pts − ptsb) −","equation_id":"(2)-(3)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"s.t. \\sum_{b\\in B}p^{t}_{sb}\\leqslant P^{t}_{s} : \\upsilon^{t}_{s}, \\forall t\\in T \\quad (2)\np^{t}_{sb}\\geqslant 0 : \\omega^{t}_{sb}, \\forall b\\in B, \\forall t\\in T \\quad (3)","paper":"49-residential_shared_storage_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"s.t. \\sum_{b\\in B}p^{t}_{sb}\\leqslant P^{t}_{s} : \\upsilon^{t}_{s}, \\forall t\\in T \\quad (2)\np^{t}_{sb}\\geqslant 0 : \\omega^{t}_{sb}, \\forall b\\in B, \\forall t\\in T \\quad (3)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E21","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p02-c1r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"Nomenclature","anchor_text":"Indices and sets V B Set of energy buyers pts S Set of energy sellers b The index of energy buyers ρ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Indices and sets B Set of energy buyers S Set of energy sellers b The index of energy buyers s The index of energy sellers T Set of time periods t Index of time periods Parameters \\Delta t Duration of period \\lambda^{t}_{sell} Feed-in Tariff in period t \\lambda^{t}_{cost} P2P transaction cost in period t \\lambda^{t}_{buy} The TLOU price of energy buyer b in period t \\lambda^{t}_{buy0} Initial electricity price in TLOU in period t k^{t} Constant coefficient in TLOU P^{t}_{s} The energy supply of seller s in period t D^{t}_{b} The energy demand of buyer b in period t \\eta_{c} Charging efficiency \\eta_{d} Discharging efficiency p^{u} Maximal charging/discharging power Q^{0}_{b} Initial energy storage level of buyer b Q_{m} Capacity of the shared energy storage units Variables p^{t}_{sb} P2P transaction amount between seller s and buyer b in period t \\rho^{t}_{sb} P2P transaction price between seller s and buyer b in period t p^{t}_{bg} Energy from the grid of buyer b in period t p^{t}_{bc} Charging power of buyer b in period t p^{t}_{bd} Discharging power of buyer b in period t Q_{b} Capacity allocation of buyer b Q^{t}_{b} Energy storage level of buyer b in period t","paper":"49-residential_shared_storage_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"Indices and sets B Set of energy buyers S Set of energy sellers b The index of energy buyers s The index of energy sellers T Set of time periods t Index of time periods Parameters \\Delta t Duration of period \\lambda^{t}_{sell} Feed-in Tariff in period t \\lambda^{t}_{cost} P2P transaction cost in period t \\lambda^{t}_{buy} The TLOU price of energy buyer b in period t \\lambda^{t}_{buy0} Initial electricity price in TLOU in period t k^{t} Constant coefficient in TLOU P^{t}_{s} The energy supply of seller s in period t D^{t}_{b} The energy demand of buyer b in period t \\eta_{c} Charging efficiency \\eta_{d} Discharging efficiency p^{u} Maximal charging/discharging power Q^{0}_{b} Initial energy storage level of buyer b Q_{m} Capacity of the shared energy storage units Variables p^{t}_{sb} P2P transaction amount between seller s and buyer b in period t \\rho^{t}_{sb} P2P transaction price between seller s and buyer b in period t p^{t}_{bg} Energy from the grid of buyer b in period t p^{t}_{bc} Charging power of buyer b in period t p^{t}_{bd} Discharging power of buyer b in period t Q_{b} Capacity allocation of buyer b Q^{t}_{b} Energy storage level of buyer b in period t"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1 Seller’s problem","anchor_text":"gy , pi to decision-making problem can be cast as ∑ ∑ ∑ ∑ e. max : ( ρtsbptsb + λtsell(Pts − ptsb) −","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"where p^{t}_{sb} and \\rho^{t}_{sb} are decision variables. p^{t}_{sb} is the transaction amount between seller s and buyer b in period t. \\rho^{t}_{sb} is transaction price associated with p^{t}_{sb}. However, the market-clearing price \\rho^{t}_{sb} is out of control of seller s and buyer b but is determined by the market equilibrium problem of the game. Parameter P^{t}_{s} is the renewable energy for sale of seller s in period t. Parameter \\lambda^{t}_{sell} is FiT when a seller sells its energy to the power grid. Parameter \\lambda^{t}_{cost} is the P2P transaction cost, including network tariff for using the physical grid facilities and aggregator service fee.","paper":"49-residential_shared_storage_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"where p^{t}_{sb} and \\rho^{t}_{sb} are decision variables. p^{t}_{sb} is the transaction amount between seller s and buyer b in period t. \\rho^{t}_{sb} is transaction price associated with p^{t}_{sb}. However, the market-clearing price \\rho^{t}_{sb} is out of control of seller s and buyer b but is determined by the market equilibrium problem of the game. Parameter P^{t}_{s} is the renewable energy for sale of seller s in period t. Parameter \\lambda^{t}_{sell} is FiT when a seller sells its energy to the power grid. Parameter \\lambda^{t}_{cost} is the P2P transaction cost, including network tariff for using the physical grid facilities and aggregator service fee."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E16","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.2 Buyer’s problem","anchor_text":"he ergy buyers in the P2P market. The second term is the revenue of selling an energy to the power g","equation_id":"(5)-(6)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"s.t. \\sum_{s\\in S}p^{t}_{sb}+p^{t}_{bg}+p^{t}_{bd}=D^{t}_{b}+p^{t}_{bc} : \\gamma^{t}_{b}, \\forall t\\in T \\quad (5)\np^{t}_{bg}\\geqslant 0 : \\omega^{t}_{bg}, \\forall t\\in T \\quad (6)","paper":"49-residential_shared_storage_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"s.t. \\sum_{s\\in S}p^{t}_{sb}+p^{t}_{bg}+p^{t}_{bd}=D^{t}_{b}+p^{t}_{bc} : \\gamma^{t}_{b}, \\forall t\\in T \\quad (5)\np^{t}_{bg}\\geqslant 0 : \\omega^{t}_{bg}, \\forall t\\in T \\quad (6)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p05-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.3 Aggregator","anchor_text":"Since the energy buyers use the SES, the allocation of SES use right is also a game. In practice, th","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The aggregator collects all participants’ supply and demand information and clears the P2P market. By solving the market equilibrium problem, it can provide P2P transaction price and amount between energy seller and buyer and capacity allocation among energy buyers. The aggregator can facilitate the P2P market and make sure participants benefit from the market.","paper":"49-residential_shared_storage_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"The aggregator collects all participants’ supply and demand information and clears the P2P market. By solving the market equilibrium problem, it can provide P2P transaction price and amount between energy seller and buyer and capacity allocation among energy buyers. The aggregator can facilitate the P2P market and make sure participants benefit from the market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E23","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p04-c2r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"1.3 Contributions","anchor_text":"Applied Energy 308 (2022) 118400 al 2) A solution method based on Karush-Kuhn-Tucker (KKT) optimalit","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"2) A solution method based on Karush-Kuhn-Tucker (KKT) optimality condition is applied to solve the market equilibrium problem. The market equilibrium is acquired based on the KKT conditions of all participants’ optimal problems. After concatenating all KKT conditions together, the market equilibrium is cast as a mixed-integer linear program (MILP) with the complementarity conditions linearized through the Big-M method. The P2P transaction price and the amount and the SES capacity allocation are obtained from the market equilibrium. The P2P transaction price is determined by the supply and demand relationship and reflects the value of energy resources. Capacity allocation among users can ensure fairness in our definition.","paper":"49-residential_shared_storage_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"2) A solution method based on Karush-Kuhn-Tucker (KKT) optimality condition is applied to solve the market equilibrium problem. The market equilibrium is acquired based on the KKT conditions of all participants’ optimal problems. After concatenating all KKT conditions together, the market equilibrium is cast as a mixed-integer linear program (MILP) with the complementarity conditions linearized through the Big-M method. The P2P transaction price and the amount and the SES capacity allocation are obtained from the market equilibrium. The P2P transaction price is determined by the supply and demand relationship and reflects the value of energy resources. Capacity allocation among users can ensure fairness in our definition."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e034","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.1 KKT conditions / P2P price","anchor_text":"B. Zheng et al. constraints. The P2P transaction price variable ρtsb is endogenously determined and ","equation_id":"(46)-(47)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The P2P transaction price variable \\rho_{sb}^{t} is endogenously determined and the SES capacity is allocated by solving equilibrium (45). From the energy sellers’ side, according to equation (28), \\rho_{sb}^{t} can be calculated as follows: \\rho_{sb}^{t} = \\lambda_{sell}^{t} + \\lambda_{cost}^{t} + (\\upsilon_s^{t} - \\omega_{sb}^{t})/\\Delta t \\tag{46} From the energy buyers’ side, according to equation (32), \\rho_{sb}^{t} can be calculated as follows: \\rho_{sb}^{t} = -\\gamma_b^{t}/\\Delta t \\tag{47} The price in (46) and (47) are the same in the equilibrium problem (45), and thus the transaction price \\rho_{sb}^{t} mainly depends on the parameters and some dual variables.","paper":"49-residential_shared_storage_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"The P2P transaction price variable \\rho_{sb}^{t} is endogenously determined and the SES capacity is allocated by solving equilibrium (45). From the energy sellers’ side, according to equation (28), \\rho_{sb}^{t} can be calculated as follows: \\rho_{sb}^{t} = \\lambda_{sell}^{t} + \\lambda_{cost}^{t} + (\\upsilon_s^{t} - \\omega_{sb}^{t})/\\Delta t \\tag{46} From the energy buyers’ side, according to equation (32), \\rho_{sb}^{t} can be calculated as follows: \\rho_{sb}^{t} = -\\gamma_b^{t}/\\Delta t \\tag{47} The price in (46) and (47) are the same in the equilibrium problem (45), and thus the transaction price \\rho_{sb}^{t} mainly depends on the parameters and some dual variables."}],"candidate_only":true,"classification_subtypes":["equilibrium_allocation_and_scarcity_outcome"],"projection_statuses":["composite"],"taxonomy":{"primary_family":"kind-L5-bb58144a46","secondary_families":[],"stage":"L5","ontological_kind":"equilibrium_allocation_and_scarcity_outcome"},"semantic_definition":{},"source_units":[{"unit_id":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-a-M01::clearing.local","paper_id":"49-residential_shared_storage_market","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"clearing.local","source_occurrences":[{"id":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","market_meaning":"The aggregator performs local P2P market clearing. Scope: Proposed local P2P energy market embedded with residential shared energy storage. In these scarcity examples, buyers offering higher P2P transaction prices acquire the limited energy. Scope: Reported Case 3 market-equilibrium examples at t = 8 and t = 18. Condition: Total buyer energy demand exceeds total energy supply, and buyers compete for limited energy. A seller’s total P2P transaction amount cannot exceed its initial surplus energy in that period. Scope: Each energy seller and each period in the proposed P2P equilibrium model. Bilateral P2P transaction amounts must be nonnegative. Scope: Every seller–buyer P2P transaction amount in every period. P2P purchases plus grid purchases plus SES discharge must equal the buyer’s energy demand plus SES charging; grid purchases must be nonnegative. Scope: Each energy buyer and each period in the proposed P2P equilibrium model.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Each energy buyer and each period in the proposed P2P equilibrium model. | Each energy seller and each period in the proposed P2P equilibrium model. | Every seller–buyer P2P transaction amount in every period. | Proposed local P2P energy market embedded with residential shared energy storage. | Reported Case 3 market-equilibrium examples at t = 8 and t = 18.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g03-e12","v141-b-g03-e13"]},"constraint_refs":["49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C001","49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C002","49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C003","49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C004","49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C005"],"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","source_rule_sha256":"5b0a6ea74646d677bac9ef5735b8532211f481cb19f837d9ad545e0e8fd0cc2c"},{"id":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R008::V::clearing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","market_meaning":"Solving the local market equilibrium determines P2P transaction allocations and produces the endogenous bilateral transaction prices. Scope: Bilateral seller–buyer transactions in the proposed local P2P market embedded with residential shared energy storage. The P2P transaction price must be no less than the feed-in tariff plus the P2P transaction cost and no greater than TLOU. Scope: Bilateral P2P transaction prices in the proposed model. No single participant unilaterally controls the P2P clearing price. Scope: The proposed local P2P pricing mechanism.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Bilateral P2P transaction prices in the proposed model. | Bilateral seller–buyer transactions in the proposed local P2P market embedded with residential shared energy storage. | The proposed local P2P pricing mechanism.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g03-e03","v141-b-g03-e04"]},"constraint_refs":["49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C001"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"cb8bb8165d1e8d357b66c34b44b5c95ee431f6bab35f04fb44df80f24044ce4d"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The aggregator performs local P2P market clearing. Scope: Proposed local P2P energy market embedded with residential shared energy storage.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09"],"ref":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p05-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.3 Aggregator","anchor_text":"Since the energy buyers use the SES, the allocation of SES use right is also a game. In practice, th","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The aggregator collects all participants’ supply and demand information and clears the P2P market. By solving the market equilibrium problem, it can provide P2P transaction price and amount between energy seller and buyer and capacity allocation among energy buyers. The aggregator can facilitate the P2P market and make sure participants benefit from the market."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C002","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"In these scarcity examples, buyers offering higher P2P transaction prices acquire the limited energy. Scope: Reported Case 3 market-equilibrium examples at t = 8 and t = 18. Condition: Total buyer energy demand exceeds total energy supply, and buyers compete for limited energy.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-e12","v141-b-g03-e13"],"ref":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p10-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":10,"printed_page":null,"section":"5.2.2 Peer-to-peer market equilibrium","anchor_text":"m. as shown in Fig. 3c. However, during the generation peak time, total al supply exceeds total dema","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-10.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"To further show the results of P2P transactions, we pick up 4 typical periods to analyze the P2P market equilibrium in Case 3, as shown in Table 4. The transaction pair is (ρ^{t}_{sb}, p^{t}_{st}), indicating the P2P transaction price and amount between seller s and buyer b during period t. The supply is the PV generation, while the demand is the initial fixed demand plus/minus charging/discharging power of shared energy storage. TLOU0 is the base price faced by buyers when purchasing electricity from the grid. FiT is the Feed-in Tariff offered by the grid. In our model, the P2P transaction price and amount are obtained from solving the market equilibrium problem."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e13","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p10-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":10,"printed_page":null,"section":"5.2.2 Peer-to-peer market equilibrium","anchor_text":"market equilibrium problem. Table 4 provides a direct insight into how ac market equilibrium arises.","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-10.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"When t = 8, the PV generation is small, so the total energy demand among energy buyers exceeds the total energy supply. In such a circumstance, all buyers will compete for the limited energy resource. Buyers offering higher transaction prices will acquire the limited energy, e.g., B3 with the highest price 0.1814. Actually, the price 0.1814 is also the marginal cost when B3 buys electricity from the grid to satisfy the unmet needs after the P2P transaction. The same analysis works at t = 18 time period."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"A seller’s total P2P transaction amount cannot exceed its initial surplus energy in that period. Scope: Each energy seller and each period in the proposed P2P equilibrium model.","expression":"\\sum_{b\\in B} p^{t}_{sb} \\le P^{t}_{s}, \\quad \\forall t\\in T","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R001-x-psb"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R001-theta-Ps"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E21"],"ref":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E14","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1 Seller’s problem","anchor_text":"he ergy buyers in the P2P market. The second term is the revenue of selling an energy to the power g","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"restatement"},"source_text":"The objective of each energy seller is to maximize its profit. In the objective function (1), the first term is the revenue of trading with energy buyers in the P2P market. The second term is the revenue of selling energy to the power grid in the FiT scheme. After participating in the P2P transaction, energy seller can still sell their surplus to the power grid to get more income. The third term is the transaction cost for P2P transactions. Constraint (2) stipulates that total P2P transaction amounts in period t should not exceed the seller’s initial excessive energy. Constraint (3) is for the non-negativity condition for the decision variable p^{t}_{sb}. \\upsilon^{t}_{s} and \\omega^{t}_{sb} after the colon are dual variables of the constraints."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1 Seller’s problem","anchor_text":"gy , pi to decision-making problem can be cast as ∑ ∑ ∑ ∑ e. max : ( ρtsbptsb + λtsell(Pts − ptsb) −","equation_id":"(2)-(3)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"s.t. \\sum_{b\\in B}p^{t}_{sb}\\leqslant P^{t}_{s} : \\upsilon^{t}_{s}, \\forall t\\in T \\quad (2)\np^{t}_{sb}\\geqslant 0 : \\omega^{t}_{sb}, \\forall b\\in B, \\forall t\\in T \\quad (3)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E21","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p02-c1r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"Nomenclature","anchor_text":"Indices and sets V B Set of energy buyers pts S Set of energy sellers b The index of energy buyers ρ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Indices and sets B Set of energy buyers S Set of energy sellers b The index of energy buyers s The index of energy sellers T Set of time periods t Index of time periods Parameters \\Delta t Duration of period \\lambda^{t}_{sell} Feed-in Tariff in period t \\lambda^{t}_{cost} P2P transaction cost in period t \\lambda^{t}_{buy} The TLOU price of energy buyer b in period t \\lambda^{t}_{buy0} Initial electricity price in TLOU in period t k^{t} Constant coefficient in TLOU P^{t}_{s} The energy supply of seller s in period t D^{t}_{b} The energy demand of buyer b in period t \\eta_{c} Charging efficiency \\eta_{d} Discharging efficiency p^{u} Maximal charging/discharging power Q^{0}_{b} Initial energy storage level of buyer b Q_{m} Capacity of the shared energy storage units Variables p^{t}_{sb} P2P transaction amount between seller s and buyer b in period t \\rho^{t}_{sb} P2P transaction price between seller s and buyer b in period t p^{t}_{bg} Energy from the grid of buyer b in period t p^{t}_{bc} Charging power of buyer b in period t p^{t}_{bd} Discharging power of buyer b in period t Q_{b} Capacity allocation of buyer b Q^{t}_{b} Energy storage level of buyer b in period t"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C004","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Bilateral P2P transaction amounts must be nonnegative. Scope: Every seller–buyer P2P transaction amount in every period.","expression":"p^{t}_{sb} \\ge 0, \\quad \\forall b\\in B,\\ \\forall t\\in T","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R001-x-psb"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E21"],"ref":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1 Seller’s problem","anchor_text":"gy , pi to decision-making problem can be cast as ∑ ∑ ∑ ∑ e. max : ( ρtsbptsb + λtsell(Pts − ptsb) −","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"where p^{t}_{sb} and \\rho^{t}_{sb} are decision variables. p^{t}_{sb} is the transaction amount between seller s and buyer b in period t. \\rho^{t}_{sb} is transaction price associated with p^{t}_{sb}. However, the market-clearing price \\rho^{t}_{sb} is out of control of seller s and buyer b but is determined by the market equilibrium problem of the game. Parameter P^{t}_{s} is the renewable energy for sale of seller s in period t. Parameter \\lambda^{t}_{sell} is FiT when a seller sells its energy to the power grid. Parameter \\lambda^{t}_{cost} is the P2P transaction cost, including network tariff for using the physical grid facilities and aggregator service fee."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E14","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1 Seller’s problem","anchor_text":"he ergy buyers in the P2P market. The second term is the revenue of selling an energy to the power g","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"restatement"},"source_text":"The objective of each energy seller is to maximize its profit. In the objective function (1), the first term is the revenue of trading with energy buyers in the P2P market. The second term is the revenue of selling energy to the power grid in the FiT scheme. After participating in the P2P transaction, energy seller can still sell their surplus to the power grid to get more income. The third term is the transaction cost for P2P transactions. Constraint (2) stipulates that total P2P transaction amounts in period t should not exceed the seller’s initial excessive energy. Constraint (3) is for the non-negativity condition for the decision variable p^{t}_{sb}. \\upsilon^{t}_{s} and \\omega^{t}_{sb} after the colon are dual variables of the constraints."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1 Seller’s problem","anchor_text":"gy , pi to decision-making problem can be cast as ∑ ∑ ∑ ∑ e. max : ( ρtsbptsb + λtsell(Pts − ptsb) −","equation_id":"(2)-(3)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"s.t. \\sum_{b\\in B}p^{t}_{sb}\\leqslant P^{t}_{s} : \\upsilon^{t}_{s}, \\forall t\\in T \\quad (2)\np^{t}_{sb}\\geqslant 0 : \\omega^{t}_{sb}, \\forall b\\in B, \\forall t\\in T \\quad (3)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E21","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p02-c1r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"Nomenclature","anchor_text":"Indices and sets V B Set of energy buyers pts S Set of energy sellers b The index of energy buyers ρ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Indices and sets B Set of energy buyers S Set of energy sellers b The index of energy buyers s The index of energy sellers T Set of time periods t Index of time periods Parameters \\Delta t Duration of period \\lambda^{t}_{sell} Feed-in Tariff in period t \\lambda^{t}_{cost} P2P transaction cost in period t \\lambda^{t}_{buy} The TLOU price of energy buyer b in period t \\lambda^{t}_{buy0} Initial electricity price in TLOU in period t k^{t} Constant coefficient in TLOU P^{t}_{s} The energy supply of seller s in period t D^{t}_{b} The energy demand of buyer b in period t \\eta_{c} Charging efficiency \\eta_{d} Discharging efficiency p^{u} Maximal charging/discharging power Q^{0}_{b} Initial energy storage level of buyer b Q_{m} Capacity of the shared energy storage units Variables p^{t}_{sb} P2P transaction amount between seller s and buyer b in period t \\rho^{t}_{sb} P2P transaction price between seller s and buyer b in period t p^{t}_{bg} Energy from the grid of buyer b in period t p^{t}_{bc} Charging power of buyer b in period t p^{t}_{bd} Discharging power of buyer b in period t Q_{b} Capacity allocation of buyer b Q^{t}_{b} Energy storage level of buyer b in period t"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C005","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"P2P purchases plus grid purchases plus SES discharge must equal the buyer’s energy demand plus SES charging; grid purchases must be nonnegative. Scope: Each energy buyer and each period in the proposed P2P equilibrium model.","expression":"\\sum_{s\\in S} p^{t}_{sb} + p^{t}_{bg} + p^{t}_{bd} = D^{t}_{b} + p^{t}_{bc}, \\quad \\forall t\\in T; \\qquad p^{t}_{bg} \\ge 0, \\quad \\forall t\\in T","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R001-x-psb","v141-c-R001-x-pbg","v141-c-R001-x-pbc","v141-c-R001-x-pbd"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R001-theta-Db"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g01-E21"],"ref":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C005","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E16","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.2 Buyer’s problem","anchor_text":"he ergy buyers in the P2P market. The second term is the revenue of selling an energy to the power g","equation_id":"(5)-(6)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"s.t. \\sum_{s\\in S}p^{t}_{sb}+p^{t}_{bg}+p^{t}_{bd}=D^{t}_{b}+p^{t}_{bc} : \\gamma^{t}_{b}, \\forall t\\in T \\quad (5)\np^{t}_{bg}\\geqslant 0 : \\omega^{t}_{bg}, \\forall t\\in T \\quad (6)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E21","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p02-c1r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"Nomenclature","anchor_text":"Indices and sets V B Set of energy buyers pts S Set of energy sellers b The index of energy buyers ρ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Indices and sets B Set of energy buyers S Set of energy sellers b The index of energy buyers s The index of energy sellers T Set of time periods t Index of time periods Parameters \\Delta t Duration of period \\lambda^{t}_{sell} Feed-in Tariff in period t \\lambda^{t}_{cost} P2P transaction cost in period t \\lambda^{t}_{buy} The TLOU price of energy buyer b in period t \\lambda^{t}_{buy0} Initial electricity price in TLOU in period t k^{t} Constant coefficient in TLOU P^{t}_{s} The energy supply of seller s in period t D^{t}_{b} The energy demand of buyer b in period t \\eta_{c} Charging efficiency \\eta_{d} Discharging efficiency p^{u} Maximal charging/discharging power Q^{0}_{b} Initial energy storage level of buyer b Q_{m} Capacity of the shared energy storage units Variables p^{t}_{sb} P2P transaction amount between seller s and buyer b in period t \\rho^{t}_{sb} P2P transaction price between seller s and buyer b in period t p^{t}_{bg} Energy from the grid of buyer b in period t p^{t}_{bc} Charging power of buyer b in period t p^{t}_{bd} Discharging power of buyer b in period t Q_{b} Capacity allocation of buyer b Q^{t}_{b} Energy storage level of buyer b in period t"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Solving the local market equilibrium determines P2P transaction allocations and produces the endogenous bilateral transaction prices. Scope: Bilateral seller–buyer transactions in the proposed local P2P market embedded with residential shared energy storage.","expression":"\\text{Equilibrium (45) determines } p^{t}_{sb} \\text{ and } \\rho^{t}_{sb}, \\text{ with } \\rho^{t}_{sb}=\\lambda^{t}_{sell}+\\lambda^{t}_{cost}+(\\upsilon^{t}_{s}-\\omega^{t}_{sb})/\\Delta t=-\\gamma^{t}_{b}/\\Delta t","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R008-x-rho","v141-c-R008-x-p"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R008-theta-Delta-t","v141-c-R008-theta-lambda-sell","v141-c-R008-theta-lambda-cost"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g02-e034"],"ref":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p05-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.3 Aggregator","anchor_text":"Since the energy buyers use the SES, the allocation of SES use right is also a game. In practice, th","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The aggregator collects all participants’ supply and demand information and clears the P2P market. By solving the market equilibrium problem, it can provide P2P transaction price and amount between energy seller and buyer and capacity allocation among energy buyers. The aggregator can facilitate the P2P market and make sure participants benefit from the market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E23","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p04-c2r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"1.3 Contributions","anchor_text":"Applied Energy 308 (2022) 118400 al 2) A solution method based on Karush-Kuhn-Tucker (KKT) optimalit","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"2) A solution method based on Karush-Kuhn-Tucker (KKT) optimality condition is applied to solve the market equilibrium problem. The market equilibrium is acquired based on the KKT conditions of all participants’ optimal problems. After concatenating all KKT conditions together, the market equilibrium is cast as a mixed-integer linear program (MILP) with the complementarity conditions linearized through the Big-M method. The P2P transaction price and the amount and the SES capacity allocation are obtained from the market equilibrium. The P2P transaction price is determined by the supply and demand relationship and reflects the value of energy resources. Capacity allocation among users can ensure fairness in our definition."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e034","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.1 KKT conditions / P2P price","anchor_text":"B. Zheng et al. constraints. The P2P transaction price variable ρtsb is endogenously determined and ","equation_id":"(46)-(47)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The P2P transaction price variable \\rho_{sb}^{t} is endogenously determined and the SES capacity is allocated by solving equilibrium (45). From the energy sellers’ side, according to equation (28), \\rho_{sb}^{t} can be calculated as follows: \\rho_{sb}^{t} = \\lambda_{sell}^{t} + \\lambda_{cost}^{t} + (\\upsilon_s^{t} - \\omega_{sb}^{t})/\\Delta t \\tag{46} From the energy buyers’ side, according to equation (32), \\rho_{sb}^{t} can be calculated as follows: \\rho_{sb}^{t} = -\\gamma_b^{t}/\\Delta t \\tag{47} The price in (46) and (47) are the same in the equilibrium problem (45), and thus the transaction price \\rho_{sb}^{t} mainly depends on the parameters and some dual variables."}]}],"variables":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R001-x-psb","symbol":"p^{t}_{sb}","meaning":"P2P transaction amount between seller s and buyer b in period t.","kind":"operational","domain":"p^{t}_{sb} \\ge 0; s \\in S, b \\in B, t \\in T","unit":null,"indices":["s","b","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g02-e012"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-psb"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R001-x-pbg","symbol":"p^{t}_{bg}","meaning":"Energy from the grid of buyer b in period t.","kind":"operational","domain":"p^{t}_{bg} \\ge 0; b \\in B, t \\in T","unit":null,"indices":["b","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g02-e014"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-pbg"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R001-x-pbc","symbol":"p^{t}_{bc}","meaning":"Charging power of buyer b in period t.","kind":"operational","domain":"p^{t}_{bc} \\ge 0 and p^{t}_{bc} \\le p^{u}; b \\in B, t \\in T","unit":null,"indices":["b","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g02-e015"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-pbc"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R001-x-pbd","symbol":"p^{t}_{bd}","meaning":"Discharging power of buyer b in period t.","kind":"operational","domain":"p^{t}_{bd} \\ge 0 and p^{t}_{bd} \\le p^{u}; b \\in B, t \\in T","unit":null,"indices":["b","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g02-e015"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-pbd"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R008-x-rho","symbol":"\\rho^{t}_{sb}","meaning":"P2P transaction price between seller s and buyer b in period t; the market-clearing price is endogenous to the market equilibrium and is not unilaterally controlled by seller s or buyer b.","kind":"operational","domain":"Endogenous scalar price. The source supplies participation bounds but no explicit set notation: \\rho^{t}_{sb} \\ge \\lambda^{t}_{sell}+\\lambda^{t}_{cost} and \\rho^{t}_{sb} \\le TLOU.","unit":null,"indices":["s","b","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g02-e024","v141-b-g02-e034","v141-b-g03-e03"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R008::x::v141-c-R008-x-rho"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R008-x-p","symbol":"p^{t}_{sb}","meaning":"P2P transaction amount between seller s and buyer b in period t; an allocation variable determined together with the P2P transaction price by the market equilibrium.","kind":"operational","domain":"Nonnegative transaction amount; the source imposes p^{t}_{sb}\\ge 0 and \\sum_{b\\in B}p^{t}_{sb}\\le P^{t}_{s} in the seller problem.","unit":null,"indices":["s","b","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E21"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R008::x::v141-c-R008-x-p"}],"parameters":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R001-theta-Ps","symbol":"P^{t}_{s}","meaning":"The renewable energy for sale / energy supply of seller s in period t.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["s","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g02-e012"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-Ps"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R001-theta-Db","symbol":"D^{t}_{b}","meaning":"The energy demand of buyer b in period t.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["b","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g02-e014"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-Db"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R008-theta-Delta-t","symbol":"\\Delta t","meaning":"Duration of a period, used in the seller-side and buyer-side price decompositions.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g02-e034"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R008::theta::v141-c-R008-theta-Delta-t"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R008-theta-lambda-sell","symbol":"\\lambda^{t}_{sell}","meaning":"Feed-in Tariff in period t; lower-bound component for the P2P transaction price.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g03-e04"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R008::theta::v141-c-R008-theta-lambda-sell"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R008-theta-lambda-cost","symbol":"\\lambda^{t}_{cost}","meaning":"P2P transaction cost in period t, including network tariff for using physical grid facilities and aggregator service fee; lower-bound component for the P2P transaction price.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g03-e04"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R008::theta::v141-c-R008-theta-lambda-cost"}]}],"source_definitions":[{"unit_id":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-a-M01::clearing.local","stage":"L5","subtype":"equilibrium_allocation_and_scarcity_outcome","projection_status":"composite","target_definition":"Includes equilibrium allocation and instance-result properties: the aggregator solves for the market equilibrium, determines bilateral transaction quantities, and allocates buyer SES capacity; the transaction quantities satisfy \\sum_{b\\in B}p^t_{sb}\\le P^t_s, p^t_{sb}\\ge0, and \\sum_{s\\in S}p^t_{sb}+p^t_{bg}+p^t_{bd}=D^t_b+p^t_{bc}, p^t_{bg}\\ge0. Additionally, in a supply-scarcity instance, buyers with higher transaction prices obtain limited electrical energy.","form_kind":"mathematical","identity_fields":["Allocation object: bilateral P2P transaction quantities and buyer SES capacity","Core allocation relation: the market equilibrium composed of each agent's optimality conditions, and the resource feasibility constraints","Allocation output: transaction quantities and capacity allocation","Independent result property: in a scarcity instance, higher-price buyers obtain limited electrical energy"],"variation_fields":["Initial seller residual quantity P^t_s and buyer demand D^t_b","Buyer grid electricity purchases and SES charging and discharging jointly enter the energy balance","The source text uses concatenation of KKT conditions, Big-M linearization, and MILP solving","The scarcity result is limited to t=8 and t=18 of Case 3","The unit does not expand the SES capacity-allocation constraints"],"constraint_refs":["49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C001","49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C002","49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C003","49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C004","49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C005","49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C001"],"paper_id":"49-residential_shared_storage_market","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"clearing.local","template_code":"BCT"}],"source_variants":[],"functional":{"is_child":false,"subdivision_pending":false},"canonical_pointer":"/nodes/96"});
